resultJson.description:
`web/src/main/scala/net/wiringbits/components/pages/BankStatementReviewPage.scala` is about 1,100 lines and holds two objects. `BankStatementReviewPage` contains the route entry, about 20 pure row-classification helpers, the `ReviewData` model with its parallel fetch, and the `AsyncComponent` wrapper. `BankStatementReviewContent` is one component of about 700 lines. It holds all page state, the AI-suggestion polling effect, the single-row and bulk action handlers, and one large render: header, filter tabs, bulk bar, error line, rows table, bulk results list, and a right-hand drawer that hosts the existing `BankRowCreateExpenseForm`, `BankRowCreateRefundForm`, `BankRowLinkPicker` and `BankRowRuleForm` components. This epic splits that file into small, cohesive units, each in its own file in the same package (`net.wiringbits.components.pages`):
- a pure logic object with no React, plus its unit spec;
- a slim loader page;
- a slim content parent that owns the state and passes data and callbacks down;
- named presentational sub-components for the header, filter tabs, bulk bar, bulk results, rows table and drawer.

This is a strict, behaviour-preserving refactor. The DOM structure, MUI styling (`CSSPropertiesUtils` values), copy, API calls, state transitions, toast messages, polling cadence, URL `?tab=` handling and memoisation must all stay identical. That includes the stable `useCallback` callbacks that keep the memoised `BankStatementReviewRow` from re-rendering. No server, endpoint, model, evolution, `ReconciliationMatcher` or bulk link-or-create semantics change. Where the old code layered one thing inside another (e.g. the tabs live inside the header's padding Box, and the bulk-results list lives inside the table's scroll Box after the Table), the parent keeps those wrapper Boxes so the rendered tree is unchanged. Sub-components return a `Fragment` or the same element the old code produced.

The work is done when `BankStatementReviewPage.scala` holds only the route entry and loader, each region of the page is a readable `FunctionalComponent` + `Props` used by the parent (no dead components), the existing pure-logic tests point at the new logic object, `CI=true sbt web/Test/compile` passes, and the targeted web specs pass.

tasks.description:
Move `object BankStatementReviewContent` (with its Props, the `SuggestionsPollMaxAttempts`/`SuggestionsPollIntervalMs` constants and the whole component body) from `BankStatementReviewPage.scala` to a new `BankStatementReviewContent.scala`. Make no logic changes.

Afterwards, `BankStatementReviewPage.scala` should contain only:
- the route entry (`apply`, `Props`, `component`), with its invalid-id message;
- the five-way parallel `fetch` (the futures start before the for-comprehension; keep it that way);
- the toast and bulk progress/results state hoisted above the remount, plus `showToast`;
- `ReviewData`, the `BulkProgress`/`BulkResults`/`RowEdits` type aliases, and `statementMetadataLine` (until the header task moves it);
- the `AsyncComponent` wrapper (`withKey(timesRefreshing.toString)`, `watchedObjects = List(timesRefreshing)`) and the Snackbar.

Remove from each file any imports that are no longer used there; `CI=true` enables -Werror. `AppRouter.scala` keeps calling `BankStatementReviewPage(props.ctx, user)` and needs no change.

Verify with `CI=true sbt web/Test/compile` and the review specs (`*BankStatementReviewLogicSpec *BankStatementReviewRowSpec`).
